' /product/model-context-layer/ — how one question is answered, including the
' case where it cannot be. The refusal branch is the point of the diagram: the
' closed world assumption is a visible path, not a claim in the prose.
@startuml
!include theme.puml
hide footbox

participant "Analyst" as U
participant "AI assistant" as A
participant "Contour MCP" as M
participant "Semantic model" as S
participant "Source systems" as D

group <b>The model describes the question
  U -> A: asks in plain language
  A -> M: calls a typed operation
  M -> S: resolves entities, metrics,\nrelationships
  S -> D: read only, entitlements applied
  D --> S: records
  S --> M: value
  M --> A: value **+ lineage**\n(the operations that produced it)
  M --> A: **+ provenance**\n(the records they read)
  A --> U: an answer that traces to source
end

group <b>The question falls outside the model
  U -> A: asks in plain language
  A -> M: calls a typed operation
  M --> A: <color:#1E40AF>no operation covers this
  A --> U: <color:#1E40AF>says it does not know
end
@enduml
